{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 (weighted fusion, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, multiprofile) is the current best at 0.525 acc / 0.498 F1, showing weighted fusion beats concat by ~1.3% acc. The largest untested lever for improving accuracy within this proven architecture is the image encoder—ResNet50 is a mid-tier backbone while ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L is substantially more expressive. Uncertainty: we don't yet know whether the image modality is underperforming due to a weak encoder or whether it simply contributes limited signal. This experiment (config_031) is a clean single-variable upgrade from config_004: only the image encoder changes (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l), keeping weighted fusion, scgpt, avgpool, and multiprofile fixed. If ViT-L yields a meaningful accuracy gain, it justifies further investment in stronger multimodal configurations; if it does not, we can redirect budget toward RNA-encoder improvements or single-modality baselines. Cost: ViT-L is a larger model than ResNet50, so expected training cost is roughly 6–7 GPU hours (vs. 4.42 for config_004), making it moderately more expensive but still well within budget for 7 remaining experiments."
}

